WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:05.379
Under Title 19 CFR, incomplete commercial invoices routinely stall cargo release at U.S. ports.

2
00:00:06.250 --> 00:00:11.396
19 CFR § 142.3 requires CBP Form 3461, right-to-make-entry proof, and a compliant invoice.

3
00:00:12.250 --> 00:00:17.690
19 CFR § 141.86 mandates port of entry, exact descriptions, currency, itemized charges, origin, and assists.

4
00:00:18.250 --> 00:00:23.391
Vague descriptions trigger CBP holds, and § 111.23 requires five-year U.S. record retention.

5
00:00:24.250 --> 00:00:29.391
Audit every § 141.86 invoice field before filing entry. Practice live citations in CodeDrill.
